    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d467">

                <pb facs="0567" n="493" xml:id="pg493"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1373</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-03T18:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 3, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7128. There is reason to believe that British cable censor has recently
                    suppressed messages in code passing between the Russian Ambassador here and the
                    Russian Ambassador in Paris.</p>
                <p>Please ascertain and report for our confidential information attitude of British
                    Government towards these Russian officials. The Department has confidence in
                    Russian Ambassador here and grants him unrestricted cable privileges.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
